  "body": "## Summary\n- freeze independent SCAN Engine v0.25 under Anchor with bounded concurrent Clang output handling and deterministic filtered recovery\n- retain the v0.24 adaptive TypeScript/React/Electron workbench as inert secondary output\n- publish reproducible source/wheel artifacts, deterministic/cache receipts, and sealed NotepadNext calibration evidence\n- keep Hermes opt-in reference-only, preserve v0.23/v0.24 unchanged, and leave H-001 uninspected\n\n## Verification\n- 140 passed, 3 Windows symlink-privilege skips in development and clean extracted package\n- package self-audit 83/83; fresh Python 3.13.13 wheel install; 12/12 LLM-disabled qualification queries\n- two cold 1,928-file scans: 21/21 byte-identical outputs and zero canonical row differences\n- cache proof: 4,186 hits, 0 misses, no canonical/workbench drift\n- final certification: 12/12 files verified, zero issues; canonical projections and database rows match the cold baseline\n\n## Calibration decision\nMechanical certification PASS; PR5 calibration remains PARTIAL. The next admissible work is generic human-surface denominator refinement, not NotepadNext-specific rules.",
